## 3. `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths` mis-parses a path whose directory contains `-of-`

**Responsibility.** Resolve any shard path to the ordered shard list.

**Problem.** `any.rfind(tag)` finds the *last* `-of-`, but the digit checks (`any[at-6] != '-'`, five digits before/after, `.gguf` at `at+9`) are positional. A path like `/data/model-of-2024-00001-of-00002.gguf` has a second `-of-` whose `at-6` is `'4'` (from `2024`), so it returns `{any}` — silently treating a split model as one shard. The check should anchor on the *filename*, not the whole path.

**Change.**

```diff
 inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
     static const char tag[] = "-of-";
-    const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
+    const size_t slash = any.find_last_of("/\\");
+    const size_t base = slash == std::string::npos ? 0 : slash + 1;
+    const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
     // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf": five digits before the tag, five after it, then the extension
-    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < base + 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
         any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
         return {any};
```

**Verification.**
1. `/tmp/x-of-2024-00001-of-00002.gguf` (both shards present) → returns the two rewritten paths, not the input.
2. `/tmp/plain.gguf` and `/tmp/a-of-b.gguf` → return `{any}` unchanged.

